1
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:14,531
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

2
00:00:14,577 --> 00:00:21,307
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

3
00:00:22,717 --> 00:00:30,048
The first verses revealed to Rasool Allah ﷺ were, the verses of Surah Al-Alaq(سورة العلق),

4
00:00:30,246 --> 00:00:32,199
the first verses of Surah Al-Alaq(سورة العلق).

5
00:00:33,615 --> 00:00:40,794
اِقْرَأْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ۝خَلَقَ الْإِنْسَانَ مِنْ عَلَقٍ۝

6
00:00:41,056 --> 00:00:51,544
اقْرَأْ وَرَبُّكَ الْأَكْرَمُ۝الَّذِي عَلَّمَ بِالْقَلَمِ۝عَلَّمَ الْإِنْسَانَ مَا لَمْ يَعْلَمْ۝

7
00:00:51,915 --> 00:00:53,799
These are the first Ayaat(آيات) that were revealed.

8
00:00:54,686 --> 00:01:02,149
After that the revelation stopped for a while.

9
00:01:02,941 --> 00:01:12,702
And the whole initial encounter of Rasool Allah ﷺ with revelation plus the waiting period that followed it,

10
00:01:13,392 --> 00:01:19,582
was to make Rasool Allah ﷺ love the revelation and miss it.

11
00:01:20,303 --> 00:01:28,434
And it is to leave permanent marks on him, or a permanent impression on him ﷺ.

12
00:01:28,497 --> 00:01:32,102
Because we mentioned that the manner in which the revelation occurred.

13
00:01:33,072 --> 00:01:39,814
Rasool Allah ﷺ was squeezed, and the same command was repeated three times.

14
00:01:40,818 --> 00:01:46,810
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ had to wait and he was missing the revelation so much.

15
00:01:47,564 --> 00:01:53,774
There's a narration Bukhari(بخاريْ) that Rasool Allah ﷺ, he missed the revelation so much

16
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:58,939
 that he would go to a top of a mountain and attempt suicide.

17
00:01:59,445 --> 00:02:04,107
The first Ayaat(آيات) that were revealed after Al-Alaq(ألعلق),

18
00:02:04,999 --> 00:02:07,840
were the Ayaat(آيات) from Surah(سورة) Al-Muzzammil(المزمل) and Sura Al-Mudassir(سورت المدثر).

19
00:02:08,336 --> 00:02:11,411
Now there's a difference of opinion on which was the first

20
00:02:11,942 --> 00:02:18,125
but there is an agreement that these were the second and third set of Ayaat(آيات)

21
00:02:18,932 --> 00:02:22,022
even though we don't know, which one of them was second or third.

22
00:02:22,768 --> 00:02:25,927
So, you have the Ayaat(آيات) of Surah Al-Alaq(سورة العلق),

23
00:02:26,641 --> 00:02:31,272
and then you have the Al-Ayaat(آيات) of Al-Muzammil(المزمل), and Ayaat(آيات) of Al-Muddassir(المدثر).

24
00:02:32,288 --> 00:02:40,181
These Ayaat(آيات), one can say that they form manual book for the Dai'yah(داعيه), the one, who was calling to Islam.

25
00:02:41,577 --> 00:02:46,132
And we can summarize it in Iqra'a(إقْرَاء), Qumm(قُمْ), Qumm(قُمْ).

26
00:02:46,813 --> 00:02:50,209
And you can remember this, Iqra'a(إقْرَاء), Qumm(قُمْ), Qumm(قُمْ),

27
00:02:51,185 --> 00:02:58,108
These were the first Ayaat(آيات) to train the early Muslims in Da'wah(دعوة).

28
00:02:58,677 --> 00:03:00,710
Iqra'a(إقْرَاء), Qumm(قُمْ), Qumm(قُمْ).

29
00:03:01,290 --> 00:03:02,117
Iqra'a(اقراء):

30
00:03:02,562 --> 00:03:10,001
اِقْرَأْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ۝ خَلَقَ الْإِنْسَانَ مِنْ عَلَقٍ۝

31
00:03:10,423 --> 00:03:11,033
Qumm: (قُمْ)

32
00:03:11,525 --> 00:03:19,911
يَا أَيُّهَا الْمُزَّمِّلُ۝قُمِ اللَّيْلَ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا۝

33
00:03:20,306 --> 00:03:21,816
And then other Qumm: (قُمْ) is:

34
00:03:22,673 --> 00:03:29,388
يَا أَيُّهَا الْمُدَّثِّرُ۝قُمْ فَأَنْذِرْ۝

35
00:03:30,459 --> 00:03:31,467
So, you have Iqra'a(إقْرَاء)

36
00:03:32,154 --> 00:03:34,130
which is command to recite and learn.

37
00:03:35,266 --> 00:03:36,188
And then you have:

38
00:03:36,918 --> 00:03:38,379
قُمِ اللَّيْلَ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا َ

39
00:03:38,742 --> 00:03:42,050
Pray at night, and then you have:

40
00:03:42,264 --> 00:03:43,478
قُمْ فَأَنْذِرْ۝

41
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:45,478
Stand up and warn.

42
00:03:47,272 --> 00:03:51,187
So, the first thing is you learn and this is something that you can apply in yourself.

43
00:03:51,609 --> 00:03:56,908
 The first thing is you learn, you study, you gain knowledge in religion.

44
00:03:58,057 --> 00:04:08,463
And then the next step is you apply this in yourself and you start preaching it to others.

45
00:04:08,503 --> 00:04:09,564
قُمْ فَأَنْذِرْ۝

46
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:12,660
Warn, so what you learn you have to teach.

47
00:04:13,060 --> 00:04:14,493
Ibn Al-Qayyim(ابن القيم) says that,

48
00:04:14,826 --> 00:04:19,267
you don't attain complete Eeman(ايمان) until you go through the stages of learning and teaching

49
00:04:19,937 --> 00:04:22,286
and propagating the message of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

50
00:04:22,782 --> 00:04:27,036
So, you have the first stage is Iqra'a(إقْرَاء) learning and then after that you start by teaching

51
00:04:27,159 --> 00:04:27,933
 قُمْ فَأَنْذِرْ۝

52
00:04:28,111 --> 00:04:29,471
Stand up and warn

53
00:04:30,098 --> 00:04:37,833
Now, learning and warning or teaching, need something else to go along with it.

54
00:04:38,601 --> 00:04:45,065
And that is Ibadah(عباده), forms of Nawafil(نوافل) that you do, like Qiyaam-Ul-Lail(قيام اليل).

55
00:04:46,262 --> 00:04:49,103
And Qiyaam-Ul-Lail(قيام اليل) was mandatory on the early Muslims.

56
00:04:50,475 --> 00:04:55,760
Allahسبحانه وتعالى made it mandatory on the early Muslims for a few years and then that was abrogated.

57
00:04:56,319 --> 00:05:02,053
And however with the situation of Rasool Allah ﷺ, he had to pray Qiyaam-Ul-Lail(قيام اليل) it was mandatory for him,

58
00:05:02,220 --> 00:05:04,340
until he passed away, until he died,

59
00:05:04,558 --> 00:05:09,117
Rasool Allah ﷺ was praying Qiyaam-Ul-Lail(قيام اليل) and it was mandatory on him.

60
00:05:10,344 --> 00:05:12,059
So, here we have a complete program.

61
00:05:12,583 --> 00:05:15,578
You have a program of learning, knowledge

62
00:05:16,213 --> 00:05:21,465
and then a program of Daw'ah(دعوة), and a program of rituals of Ibadah(عبادة).

63
00:05:22,550 --> 00:05:30,373
And they all complement each other and they all assist in building a complete Muslim personality.

64
00:05:31,017 --> 00:05:35,579
The work of propagating and teaching could be draining on the heart

65
00:05:35,729 --> 00:05:44,238
and without this element of Ibadah(عبادة), one standing up and praying to Allah سبحانه وتعالى, in the middle of the night

66
00:05:44,731 --> 00:05:47,649
the heart could harshen and become rough.

67
00:05:48,166 --> 00:05:51,480
So, this Qiyaam-Ul-Lail(قيام اليل) softens the heart

68
00:05:52,365 --> 00:05:55,337
and it prepares the person for the rest of the day.

69
00:05:56,003 --> 00:05:57,842
Such thing can also be said about Zikr(زكر),

70
00:05:58,522 --> 00:06:01,129
Ibn Qayyim(ابن القيم), he talks about his Shaikh Ibn Taymiyyah(شيخ ابن تيميه).

71
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:09,662
He says that every day after Salaat-Ul-Fajr(صلاة الفجر), he would go out to the fields in the outskirts of Damascus.

72
00:06:10,611 --> 00:06:16,263
And he would just sit there mentioning the name of Allah making Zikr(زكر) until sunrise.

73
00:06:17,247 --> 00:06:20,103
So, we once told him, why do you do this on a daily basis.

74
00:06:20,143 --> 00:06:25,694
Ibn Taymiyyah(ابن تيميه) said: This is my breakfast, if I don't have it, my body will fail me.

75
00:06:26,790 --> 00:06:31,700
This is food for my soul, it gives me energy for the rest of the day.

76
00:06:32,496 --> 00:06:37,204
If I don't have this meal in the morning, I'm going to be weak for the rest of my day.

77
00:06:38,509 --> 00:06:42,424
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was strengthened by this Ibadah(عبادة) of the Qiyaam-Ul-Lail(قيام اليل).

78
00:06:42,932 --> 00:06:46,130
And it is also something that Allah made mandatory on the early Muslims,

79
00:06:46,210 --> 00:06:49,428
because of the unique circumstances they went through,

80
00:06:49,780 --> 00:06:55,943
the difficulties that they had to go through are more than anything else that the Ummah(امة) would face afterwards.

81
00:06:56,273 --> 00:06:58,940
That's why they had to go through this intensive training.

82
00:06:59,551 --> 00:07:03,772
Plus, they are the core group, they are the foundation of Islam.

83
00:07:04,186 --> 00:07:11,638
Sahabah رضي الله عنهم are the generation, which Islam was built on, they are the ones who spread it,

84
00:07:11,734 --> 00:07:17,470
and if you have like a tent, there's this pillar in the middle that holds the whole tent,

85
00:07:18,002 --> 00:07:21,891
that is the Sahabah(صحابہ) for this religion, they were the foundation of this religion.

86
00:07:22,123 --> 00:07:26,863
 So, they had to be very strong, and that strength came from this intensive training program

87
00:07:27,198 --> 00:07:30,208
that they went through in the early years of Makkah.

88
00:07:30,698 --> 00:07:37,579
So, you had this core group which is small in number, we could say less than 100, who went through this training.

89
00:07:38,015 --> 00:07:42,035
 But then these people became so strong that wherever you could put them

90
00:07:42,447 --> 00:07:45,589
you could immediately see the influence they have on the people surrounding them.

91
00:07:45,985 --> 00:07:48,732
I mean, Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار), for example, are late comers to Islam,

92
00:07:49,101 --> 00:07:54,652
Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار) only became Muslim, in the last half of the Da'wah(دعوة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ .

93
00:07:55,123 --> 00:07:58,344
But because the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) came and lived with them, and mixed with them

94
00:07:58,415 --> 00:08:02,739
and in the initial stage, Rasool Allah ﷺ made the Brotherhood.

95
00:08:03,138 --> 00:08:05,817
you would have one Ansaari(أنصاري) and one Muhajir(مهاجر), and they were brothers.

96
00:08:06,454 --> 00:08:12,293
This gave a chance for the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) to help the Ansaar(أنصار) in the religious aspect

97
00:08:12,671 --> 00:08:18,873
 and the Ansaar(أنصار) helped the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) in the financial support and the social support that they needed.

98
00:08:20,133 --> 00:08:23,218
But the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم the early Sahabah(صحابہ),

99
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:31,080
the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) had this light in them that would emanate and affect the whole surrounding, around them.

100
00:08:32,489 --> 00:08:38,441
So, we have Iqra'a(إقْرَاء), Qumm(قُمْ), Qumm(قُمْ), and remember these three words.

101
00:08:40,119 --> 00:08:47,173
What was the response of the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) to the Da'wah(دعوة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

102
00:08:48,198 --> 00:08:51,830
They responded in various different ways.

103
00:08:53,466 --> 00:08:58,796
And some of them were at different times, and some of them might have been stages.

104
00:08:59,042 --> 00:09:06,155
But these are the different responses that the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), showed towards the message of Muhammadﷺ.

105
00:09:06,485 --> 00:09:10,512
And there's a list of them we'll start talking about them right now but I'll just go through the list.

106
00:09:11,059 --> 00:09:12,580
And Number one, mockery,

107
00:09:12,984 --> 00:09:15,969
Number two, insulting and harming the Messenger,

108
00:09:16,729 --> 00:09:20,800
Number three, accusations or character assassination.

109
00:09:21,598 --> 00:09:24,612
Number four, deforming or defaming the message.

110
00:09:25,894 --> 00:09:30,042
Number five, bargaining and negotiating with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

111
00:09:30,478 --> 00:09:33,868
Number six, allurements and temptations,

112
00:09:34,270 --> 00:09:36,811
Number seven, setting challenges,

113
00:09:37,507 --> 00:09:41,606
Number eight, putting Muhammadﷺ under pressure.

114
00:09:42,210 --> 00:09:44,620
Number nine, jealousy and hatred,

115
00:09:45,219 --> 00:09:46,840
Number ten, persecution,

116
00:09:47,275 --> 00:09:50,167
 and Eleven assassination attempts.

117
00:09:50,754 --> 00:09:54,096
So, In Sha Allah(إن شاءالله) we'll start with, Number one: Mockery.

118
00:09:54,579 --> 00:09:56,389
Allahسبحانه وتعالى says,

119
00:09:56,875 --> 00:10:06,760
وَإِذَا رَأَوْكَ إِنْ يَتَّخِذُونَكَ إِلَّا هُزُوًا أَهَٰذَا الَّذِي بَعَثَ اللَّهُ رَسُولًا۝

120
00:10:07,415 --> 00:10:14,086
When they see you they ridicule you and say Is this the one whom Allah has sent as a Messenger.

121
00:10:15,055 --> 00:10:23,027
They were saying, didn't Allah find anyone else to send, I mean, there was no one better to send except you?

122
00:10:23,737 --> 00:10:26,973
So, they would make fun of Rasool Allah ﷺ, they would mock at him.

123
00:10:27,738 --> 00:10:34,466
Now even though, Rasool Allah ﷺ belong to the noblest family, he had the most outstanding character in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

124
00:10:34,955 --> 00:10:40,953
But because he wasn't the wealthiest, because he wasn't the most powerful, they made fun of him.

125
00:10:41,939 --> 00:10:47,990
People are attracted to the ones, who have wealth, and the ones, who have power.

126
00:10:48,760 --> 00:10:54,029
And there's precedence in this, when the Banni Israel(بني إسرائيل) and the stories mentioned in Surah Al-Baqarah(سورة البقره),

127
00:10:54,403 --> 00:10:56,628
when Banni Israel(بني إسرائيل) went to their Prophet and they said:

128
00:10:56,879 --> 00:11:01,923
We want you to appoint a king over us so that we could fight in Jihad(جهاد).

129
00:11:02,325 --> 00:11:03,841
The King appointed Talut(طالوت),

130
00:11:04,513 --> 00:11:07,615
the Nabi(نبي) appointed Talut(طالوت) to be a king and their leader.

131
00:11:08,092 --> 00:11:13,187
They refused, even though they are the ones, who asked the Nabi(نبي) to appoint for them when the Nabi(نبي) appointed,

132
00:11:13,464 --> 00:11:18,091
they rejected and refused to accept, the leadership of Talut(طالوت).

133
00:11:18,330 --> 00:11:19,107
 Why?

134
00:11:19,620 --> 00:11:20,427
They said,

135
00:11:20,976 --> 00:11:22,544
وَلَمْ يُعْطَ سَاعَتً امِنَ الْمَالْ

136
00:11:23,521 --> 00:11:25,781
that he doesn't have a lot of money, he's not wealthy,

137
00:11:27,104 --> 00:11:31,767
اَنَّ يَكُوْنُوْ لَهُ الْمُلْكُ عَلَيْنَا وَنَحْنُ اَحَقُّ بِالُمُلْكِ مِنْهْ وَلَمْ يُعْطَ سَاعَتً امِنَ الْمَالْ

138
00:11:31,850 --> 00:11:33,900
Two things, they said: he is not wealthy.

139
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:35,671
وَنَحْنُ اَحَقُّ بِالُمُلْكِ مِنْهْ

140
00:11:35,710 --> 00:11:38,122
And there are people more prominent among us to be kings.

141
00:11:39,022 --> 00:11:41,165
And when Rasool Allah ﷺ went to At-Taef(ألطائف)

142
00:11:41,741 --> 00:11:43,596
and we'll talk about his story in At-Taef(ألطائف)

143
00:11:44,124 --> 00:11:47,950
one of the men of At-Taef(ألطائف) told Muhammadﷺ,

144
00:11:48,269 --> 00:11:51,680
didn't Allah find anyone better than you to send as a Prophet.

145
00:11:52,334 --> 00:11:56,722
So, they would mock at Muhammadﷺ and they would make fun of him.

146
00:11:57,440 --> 00:12:01,751
The second form or the second response,

147
00:12:02,235 --> 00:12:09,601
that the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) showed, was insulting and harming Muhammadﷺ.

148
00:12:11,115 --> 00:12:15,253
In Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم) Abu Hurairahرضي الله عنه narrates the story:

149
00:12:15,404 --> 00:12:21,367
Abu Jahal(ابوجهل), he came to some of the leaders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), who were sitting next to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) and he told them,

150
00:12:22,231 --> 00:12:25,452
are you allowing Muhammad(محمد) to rub his face in the dirt?

151
00:12:26,047 --> 00:12:29,117
That was his evil way of saying Sujood(سجود).

152
00:12:29,674 --> 00:12:32,807
Are you allowing Muhammad(محمد) to rub his face in the dirt?

153
00:12:33,496 --> 00:12:36,721
If I see him do that, I will trample his neck.

154
00:12:38,123 --> 00:12:43,692
If I see him do that I will trample over his neck and I will rub his face in the dirt.

155
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:50,546
When Rasool Allah ﷺ did come and he started to pray and Rasool Allah ﷺ would pray publicly in front of anyone.

156
00:12:51,001 --> 00:12:57,383
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was praying right there in front of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) and Abu Jahal(ابوجهل) and his friends saw this.

157
00:12:57,600 --> 00:13:00,649
 So, Abu Jahal(ابوجهل) stood up to go and fulfill his threat.

158
00:13:01,244 --> 00:13:05,344
So, he walked up to Muhammadﷺ and Muhammadﷺ was in Sujood(سجود)

159
00:13:06,272 --> 00:13:14,258
and suddenly they saw Abu Jahal(ابوجهل) falling back and he was waving with his hands,

160
00:13:14,484 --> 00:13:18,635
like someone who's trying to repulse a danger that is about to befall him.

161
00:13:19,908 --> 00:13:23,308
So, Abu Jahal(ابوجهل) came back and they told him, what happened to you, what was wrong?

162
00:13:23,783 --> 00:13:26,405
He says; What do you mean what happened.! Didn't you see what happened?

163
00:13:26,782 --> 00:13:32,335
They said, no we didn't, there was nothing, all what we saw is, you falling on your back and, waving your hands.

164
00:13:32,916 --> 00:13:38,207
Abu Jahal(ابوجهل) said: There was a trench in front of me, and there was fire and wings and terror.

165
00:13:38,625 --> 00:13:45,727
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Those were the angels, if he would have came any closer to me, they would have torn him into pieces.

166
00:13:47,525 --> 00:13:50,206
So, he saw that but everybody else didn't.

167
00:13:50,641 --> 00:13:52,942
All what they saw was, Abu Jahal(ابوجهل) retreating.

168
00:13:53,380 --> 00:13:57,615
And Rasool Allah ﷺ said: those were the angels they would have torn him into pieces, if he came any closer.

169
00:14:00,207 --> 00:14:05,693
Uqba Bin Abi Moyait(عقبة بن ابي معيت), one day came to Rasool Allah ﷺ next to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

170
00:14:06,266 --> 00:14:11,532
And you would notice that most of these events occur next to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) because that is where Rasool Allah ﷺ would pray publicly.

171
00:14:12,007 --> 00:14:14,492
And they would always try to stop him from doing that.

172
00:14:15,381 --> 00:14:18,390
So, Uqba Bin Abi Moyait(عقبة بن ابي معيت) walked up to Muhammadﷺ

173
00:14:18,715 --> 00:14:24,661
and he grabbed his clothes and he started wrapping them around the neck of Rasool Allah ﷺ, trying to choke him

174
00:14:25,339 --> 00:14:30,212
until, Abu Bakrرضي الله عنه stepped in and pushed Uqba Bin Abi Moyait(عقبة بن ابي معيت) away.

175
00:14:30,466 --> 00:14:35,488
And he said: Do you want to kill a man just because he says my lord is Allah.

176
00:14:36,077 --> 00:14:39,328
اَتُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ تَقْتُلُوْنَ رَجُلً اَنْ يَقًوْلَ رَبِّيَ الله

177
00:14:39,975 --> 00:14:43,279
The reason why you want to kill him is because he's saying my lord is Allah

178
00:14:43,527 --> 00:14:46,054
and he pushed Uqba Bin Abi Moyait(عقبة بن ابي معيت) away.

179
00:14:47,465 --> 00:14:54,859
Now for some people, they don't mind being hurt, or cursed or humiliated.

180
00:14:55,328 --> 00:14:59,020
 Some people naturally have thick skin, I mean, they're not sensitive at all.

181
00:14:59,737 --> 00:15:06,905
But the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah صلوات الله وسلام عليه, they were very sensitive, and they had a lot of dignity.

182
00:15:06,972 --> 00:15:08,969
 So, such things hurt them and harm them a lot.

183
00:15:09,887 --> 00:15:15,163
And the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah, they all had very respectable personalities.

184
00:15:15,656 --> 00:15:20,206
So, when such things happened, I mean, these are very, very insulting events to them.

185
00:15:20,854 --> 00:15:26,387
And this was hurting Rasool Allah ﷺ a lot, but he would continue with his Da'wah(دعوة) and go on,

186
00:15:26,756 --> 00:15:28,937
and he would follow, what Allahسبحانه وتعالى told him.

187
00:15:28,977 --> 00:15:29,998
 وَأَعْرِضْ عَنِ الْجَاهِلِينَ۝

188
00:15:30,091 --> 00:15:32,248
Just ignore the ignorant, ignore them.

189
00:15:32,620 --> 00:15:36,829
Rasool Ullah would not respond to them, would not fight with them, he would go on with his work.

190
00:15:38,511 --> 00:15:41,644
Another incident that was narrated by Al-Bukhari(اَلْبُخَارِيْ),

191
00:15:42,344 --> 00:15:50,143
Rasool Allah ﷺ again was praying next to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) and Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) came to the leaders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

192
00:15:50,281 --> 00:15:53,420
who would always meet and sit, next to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

193
00:15:54,177 --> 00:15:58,253
And he told them, so and so has slaughtered a camel,

194
00:15:58,967 --> 00:16:05,576
who will go and pick up the contents of the abdomen of the camel, and dump it on Rasool Allah ﷺ in Salah(صلاة).

195
00:16:06,487 --> 00:16:12,532
So, the most evil among them, Uqba Bin Abi Moyait(عقبة بن ابي معيت), he picked up the challenge

196
00:16:13,215 --> 00:16:21,644
and he went and grabbed all of the insides of the abdomen, the intestines and the stomach, and he carried it.

197
00:16:22,189 --> 00:16:27,066
 And he waited until Rasool Allah ﷺ was in the position of Sujood(سجود), and he dumped it over him.

198
00:16:28,739 --> 00:16:32,156
Rasool Allah ﷺ continued with his Sujood(سجود) as if nothing happened.

199
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:37,473
And then his daughter Fatima رضي الله عنها, saw what happened to her father.

200
00:16:37,749 --> 00:16:42,625
And by the way, it's very hurting to children to see their parents being humiliated,

201
00:16:43,646 --> 00:16:46,654
And psychiatrists in Falastein(فلسطين),

202
00:16:47,149 --> 00:16:52,185
they say that this is affecting the psychology of the children in Falastein(فلسطين),

203
00:16:52,479 --> 00:16:58,850
when they see their fathers and their mothers abused and kicked and hit by Israeli soldiers.

204
00:16:59,122 --> 00:17:06,741
So, you have an entire generation of children, who are growing up seeing their parents going through all of this abuse.

205
00:17:07,298 --> 00:17:14,303
And the psychiatrist was saying that it leaves some very dangerous marks and scars on their personalities.

206
00:17:14,390 --> 00:17:20,525
 I mean, especially for children, it's very detrimental for them to see their parents go through humiliation.

207
00:17:20,848 --> 00:17:23,737
So, Fatima رضي الله عنها she saw this happening to her father,

208
00:17:23,793 --> 00:17:28,262
and her father continued in Sujood(سجود), so she ran up to him

209
00:17:28,667 --> 00:17:33,877
and she started taking all of that dirt from the shoulders of her father.

210
00:17:34,821 --> 00:17:36,942
Rasool Allah ﷺ when he finished his Salaah(صلاة).

211
00:17:37,491 --> 00:17:41,856
He made a Dua(دُعَا) and he did Dua(دُعَا) publicly in front of the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

212
00:17:41,995 --> 00:17:45,134
He said: O Allah punish Abu Jahal(ابوجهل)

213
00:17:46,401 --> 00:17:47,833
and Utba Bin Rabiya(عتبة بن ربيعه)

214
00:17:48,303 --> 00:17:49,489
and Shaybah Bin Rabiya(شيبة بن ربيعه),

215
00:17:50,612 --> 00:17:51,641
Al-Waleed Bin Utbah(الوليد بن عتبة),

216
00:17:52,644 --> 00:17:53,850
Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(امية بن خلف)

217
00:17:54,755 --> 00:17:56,402
and Uqba Bin Abi Moyait(عقبة بن ابي معيت).

218
00:17:57,358 --> 00:17:58,787
He made Dua(دُعَا) against seven

219
00:17:59,245 --> 00:18:00,413
I counted six.

220
00:18:01,121 --> 00:18:05,527
The seventh Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود), the narrator of the Hadith(حديث) said I forgot, who was the seventh.

221
00:18:06,620 --> 00:18:08,586
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ made Dua(دُعَا) against them,

222
00:18:08,666 --> 00:18:13,976
and this was a very rare thing that Rasool Allah ﷺ would make Dua(دُعَا) against some people.

223
00:18:14,680 --> 00:18:18,634
But it's got so bad that Rasool Allah ﷺ was so hurt

224
00:18:19,613 --> 00:18:22,702
he made Dua(دُعَا) against them, and he made Dua(دُعَا) in front of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

225
00:18:23,559 --> 00:18:25,224
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) said,

226
00:18:26,131 --> 00:18:31,110
I have seen with my own eyes, all of these men killed in the Battle of Badr(بدر),

227
00:18:32,256 --> 00:18:32,976
all of them.

228
00:18:33,670 --> 00:18:37,829
That was the fulfillment of the Dua(دُعَا) of Rasool Allah ﷺ , they all died on Kufr(كفر).

229
00:18:39,467 --> 00:18:46,326
Now, I just gave a few examples, but there are many other examples that one could go through that illuminate this point further.

230
00:18:46,808 --> 00:18:47,674
Number three,

231
00:18:48,484 --> 00:18:54,147
Accusing the Prophet ﷺ, or what we could refer to as character assassination.

232
00:18:55,170 --> 00:19:01,651
They would try to attack the character of the messenger to destroy the message.

233
00:19:02,556 --> 00:19:06,279
So, they would accuse Rasool Allah ﷺ of being a magician,

234
00:19:06,886 --> 00:19:16,234
وَقَالُوا يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِي نُزِّلَ عَلَيْهِ الذِّكْرُ إِنَّكَ لَمَجْنُونٌ۝

235
00:19:16,850 --> 00:19:21,442
They said: O you who is receiving the revelation, you are insane.

236
00:19:22,013 --> 00:19:23,461
وَقَالَو سَاحِرٌ كَذَّابٌ۝

237
00:19:23,536 --> 00:19:28,839
They said: He's a magician, and a liar and they said he's a soothsayer, Kahin(كاهن).

238
00:19:29,208 --> 00:19:32,738
They used whatever slandering terms they could use.

239
00:19:32,777 --> 00:19:42,255
They'd just throw them at Rasool Allah ﷺ, in order to assassinate the character of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

240
00:19:42,833 --> 00:19:48,642
And the purpose of that is to destroy the message itself, because Allahسبحانه وتعالى says,

241
00:19:49,446 --> 00:19:54,920
قَدْ نَعْلَمُ إِنَّهُ لَيَحْزُنُكَ الَّذِي يَقُولُونَ ۖ

242
00:19:55,257 --> 00:20:04,711
فَإِنَّهُمْ لَا يُكَذِّبُونَكَ وَلَٰكِنَّ الظَّالِمِينَ بِآيَاتِ اللَّهِ يَجْحَدُونَ۝

243
00:20:05,809 --> 00:20:10,095
They do not disbelieve you, but they are rejecting the signs of Allah.

244
00:20:10,829 --> 00:20:14,116
Allahسبحانه وتعالى is saying that they don't really have a problem with you.

245
00:20:14,656 --> 00:20:20,060
They do not disbelieve you, deep in their hearts, they know that you are the truthful and the honest.

246
00:20:20,430 --> 00:20:23,929
 But it is because they want to reject the message, they are attacking you.

247
00:20:24,625 --> 00:20:30,230
So, all of these attacks that you are receiving is not because of your character, it is because of the religion.

248
00:20:31,501 --> 00:20:39,657
And this will take us back to the words of Warqah Bin Nofal(ورقه بن نوفل), in the early days he told Muhammadﷺ, you will be driven out of your land.

249
00:20:40,409 --> 00:20:43,701
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Me, they will drive me out of my land.?

250
00:20:44,112 --> 00:20:48,390
 Rasool Allah ﷺ knew that he was so admired and loved by the people of Makkah,

251
00:20:48,853 --> 00:20:52,285
he couldn't imagine how one day they will drive him out of his land.

252
00:20:52,309 --> 00:20:58,034
But then Warqah Bin Nofal(ورقه بن نوفل) said: Anyone who would present his people with a message similar to yours,

253
00:20:58,837 --> 00:21:02,178
would be fought he will have enemies.

254
00:21:02,619 --> 00:21:04,775
So, it's not you it is the message.

255
00:21:05,304 --> 00:21:10,098
So, now they were accusing Muhammadﷺ, in order to block the message.

256
00:21:11,062 --> 00:21:19,797
Rasool Allah ﷺ would go into the marketplace and the marketplaces in Makkah served not only as a place for doing business,

257
00:21:20,276 --> 00:21:29,355
but that's where they would hold their fairs, I'll just give the meaning of it.

258
00:21:29,565 --> 00:21:34,871
They would have competitions in poetry, and they would have competitions in speeches,

259
00:21:35,271 --> 00:21:38,594
 they would hold those competitions in these marketplaces.

260
00:21:39,368 --> 00:21:43,854
So, the marketplace wasn't strictly for business but it was also the cultural center.

261
00:21:44,875 --> 00:21:48,119
That's where the speakers would come, it's sort of like Hyde Park

262
00:21:48,866 --> 00:21:52,628
speakers from all over the world would go, and just congregate there.

263
00:21:52,866 --> 00:21:58,757
Although it was a difference, I mean in Hyde park you don't necessarily get the best but in Souq Akaaz(سوق اعكاظ) you will get the best,

264
00:21:59,370 --> 00:22:02,110
the best speakers of Arabia would go to Souq Akaaz(سوق اعكاظ)

265
00:22:02,930 --> 00:22:06,400
and they would present their works, their poetry and their speeches.

266
00:22:06,906 --> 00:22:11,898
And the best of these poems will be hang on the wall of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه),

267
00:22:12,668 --> 00:22:16,197
they are called Al-Muallaqaat(ألمعلقات), the hanged poems.

268
00:22:17,098 --> 00:22:23,358
Rasool Allah ﷺ would enter these marketplaces and speak to the masses.

269
00:22:24,405 --> 00:22:27,842
In this Hadith(حديث) narrated by Imam Al-Ahmad(امام الاحمد).

270
00:22:28,475 --> 00:22:31,622
Rabiya Bin Haddad(ربيعه بن حداد), he says that

271
00:22:31,662 --> 00:22:39,066
I saw the Messenger of Allah in the Market of Zul-Majaaz(ذوالمجاز) or the fair of Zul-Majaaz(ذوالمجاز).

272
00:22:39,335 --> 00:22:45,029
And he was saying, O, you people say there is no God but Allah and you would prosper.

273
00:22:45,607 --> 00:22:47,716
That was his message to the people say:

274
00:22:47,756 --> 00:22:49,388
 لا اله الا الله تُفْلِحُوْ

275
00:22:50,270 --> 00:22:52,863
Say there is no God but Allah and you would be successful.

276
00:22:53,339 --> 00:22:57,037
And he would repeat that message again and again and walk and meet different people.

277
00:22:57,740 --> 00:23:01,955
Now, Rabiyyah(ربيعة) said: There was a man following him.

278
00:23:03,246 --> 00:23:09,900
And whoever Rasool Allah ﷺ would speak to, this man would go and speak to, and say;

279
00:23:10,966 --> 00:23:12,960
"Don't believe him, he's a liar"

280
00:23:14,548 --> 00:23:17,647
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ would go and speak to a group of people and tell them say;

281
00:23:17,672 --> 00:23:18,465
لا اله الا الله

282
00:23:18,490 --> 00:23:19,340
you would succeed.

283
00:23:19,779 --> 00:23:23,741
When Rasool Allah leaves Abu Lahab(أبو لهب) would come in, and tell the same people,

284
00:23:23,900 --> 00:23:25,767
"Don't believe him, he's a liar."

285
00:23:26,427 --> 00:23:28,822
Now, Rabiya Bin Haddad(ربيعه بن حداد) said: I asked who that man was.

286
00:23:28,894 --> 00:23:30,535
 They said, this is his Uncle Abu Lahab(أبو لهب).

287
00:23:30,575 --> 00:23:32,178
Rabiya Bin Haddad(ربيعه بن حداد) wasn't from Makkah.

288
00:23:32,482 --> 00:23:34,266
He said, I asked who that man was?

289
00:23:34,546 --> 00:23:35,966
They said; This is his uncle.

290
00:23:37,300 --> 00:23:43,944
Imagine how difficult this is, Abu Lahab(أبو لهب) is unwinding whatever was been winded, by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

291
00:23:44,688 --> 00:23:48,627
Whatever Rasool Allah ﷺ would do, Abu Lahab(أبو لهب) would go behind him and destroy it.

292
00:23:49,810 --> 00:23:55,406
We gain encouragement, by seeing the fruits of our efforts.

293
00:23:56,805 --> 00:24:01,272
We have to be rewarded one way or another otherwise, we wouldn't have motivation to go on.

294
00:24:02,485 --> 00:24:09,268
In our work, unless there's some kind of reward, it would be impossible for us to work.

295
00:24:09,824 --> 00:24:12,606
And we are rewarded in different forms, one of them is financial

296
00:24:13,146 --> 00:24:14,427
you're being paid for what you do.

297
00:24:15,230 --> 00:24:17,496
Other forms of reward is recognition.

298
00:24:18,242 --> 00:24:24,610
Third form of reward is support that you would get from workers or your leaders.

299
00:24:25,425 --> 00:24:30,337
But it will be impossible to go on, if everything is against you at your work.

300
00:24:32,224 --> 00:24:36,511
And what keeps you going is seeing the fruits of your efforts.

301
00:24:36,901 --> 00:24:42,483
I mean, imagine that we arrange this course and it doesn't work out.

302
00:24:43,118 --> 00:24:47,156
And then we try to arrange it again a month later and it doesn't work out, nobody shows up.

303
00:24:47,360 --> 00:24:52,040
Imagine just they try it again next month, no one shows up.

304
00:24:52,466 --> 00:24:57,762
They try it again, third time no one shows up do you think they will have the spirit to continue doing this again and again,

305
00:24:58,054 --> 00:24:59,106
it becomes really difficult.

306
00:24:59,633 --> 00:25:02,907
Rasool Allah ﷺ and some of the many of the other Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء)

307
00:25:03,381 --> 00:25:06,885
they would continue doing the same thing again and again and nothing would happen.

308
00:25:08,141 --> 00:25:09,792
And Noahعليه السّلام for example.

309
00:25:10,559 --> 00:25:16,849
He's giving his people Da'wah(دعوة) day and night publicly and privately with no response, no response, whatsoever.

310
00:25:16,889 --> 00:25:19,395
He's seeing no fruits of his efforts at all.

311
00:25:20,419 --> 00:25:23,692
That's very difficult, especially when we're talking about 950 years.

312
00:25:24,688 --> 00:25:28,770
Rasool Allah ﷺ in Makkah is going and speaking to these people who don't know him.

313
00:25:29,586 --> 00:25:34,333
He's speaking to foreigners, and this fair of Zul Majaz(ذوالمجاز) and Aakaaz(أعكاظ).

314
00:25:35,359 --> 00:25:42,102
And as soon as he speaks to the people, someone comes and distorts his reputation by saying, he's a liar.

315
00:25:43,031 --> 00:25:53,520
Nevertheless, Rasool Allah ﷺ, had the encouragement to continue and speak to the people and go on and on, neglecting what his uncle was doing to him,

316
00:25:54,030 --> 00:25:57,569
especially in the society of Arabia, where there's seniority.

317
00:25:57,609 --> 00:26:00,719
 I mean, what can Rasool Allah ﷺ do to stop his uncle.

318
00:26:02,256 --> 00:26:05,915
So, he would just leave him alone and continue with his Da'wah(دعوة).

319
00:26:05,955 --> 00:26:10,732
And in another narration it says that Abu Lahab(أبو لهب) would go on and tell the people.

320
00:26:10,811 --> 00:26:17,093
O people, let not this man, entice you away from your religion, the religion of your forefathers.

321
00:26:17,417 --> 00:26:19,214
And this was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi(ألبيهقي).

322
00:26:21,198 --> 00:26:24,090
Another example narrated by Al-Bayhaqi(ألبيهقي) and Al-Hakim(الحاكم);

323
00:26:24,839 --> 00:26:31,461
Right before the season of Hajj(حج), Al-Waleed Bin Mugheera(الوليد بن مغيره), who was the elder of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) at that time,

324
00:26:32,218 --> 00:26:38,903
he addressed a meeting of the leaders of the community.

325
00:26:40,301 --> 00:26:45,164
And he told them, that the season of Hajj(حَجْ) is approaching, pilgrimage.

326
00:26:45,720 --> 00:26:48,816
And the delegations of the Arabs are going to start pouring in.

327
00:26:49,448 --> 00:26:58,475
Let's unify our opinion regarding disassociate of yours and let's not contradict each other.

328
00:26:59,667 --> 00:27:01,952
What Al-Waleed Bin Mugheera(الوليد بن مغيره) is referring to here?

329
00:27:02,614 --> 00:27:10,206
Is that the season of pilgrimage is coming and the Arabs are going to start coming to Makkah,

330
00:27:10,773 --> 00:27:14,735
and Muhammadﷺ will be visiting them and speaking to them.

331
00:27:16,084 --> 00:27:21,082
We don't want to contradict each other in our opinion regarding him.

332
00:27:21,363 --> 00:27:26,873
So, we don't want some people saying that he is a liar, some people saying is a magician, some people saying is this soothsayer

333
00:27:27,204 --> 00:27:35,027
we have to have a unified opinion in order to go to the people and warn them from this man.

334
00:27:36,153 --> 00:27:39,759
So, the people said, you tell us what you think, we'll abide by it.

335
00:27:41,267 --> 00:27:44,204
Al-Waleed Bin Mugheera(الوليد بن مغيره) said: I want to hear from you.

336
00:27:45,234 --> 00:27:48,152
They said: We'll claim that he's a soothsayer.

337
00:27:49,304 --> 00:27:52,462
He responded, No! He is no soothsayer,

338
00:27:52,846 --> 00:27:59,533
I have seen soothsayers and he doesn't engage in the rhymed mumbling Doug rail they use.

339
00:28:01,219 --> 00:28:04,545
People are not going to believe you, if you say that he's a soothsayer.

340
00:28:05,539 --> 00:28:10,023
They said: Well, let's say that he is crazy, possessed by spirits.

341
00:28:11,478 --> 00:28:12,901
He said: He is not crazy.

342
00:28:13,258 --> 00:28:15,769
We have seen and known those, who are crazy.

343
00:28:16,142 --> 00:28:20,466
And he has none of their choking, erratic movement and mumbling.

344
00:28:21,212 --> 00:28:26,936
He doesn't show the signs of people who are insane or obsessed by Jinn(جن).

345
00:28:27,738 --> 00:28:29,464
They said: Well, let's claim that he is a poet.

346
00:28:30,677 --> 00:28:32,146
He said: No, he's no poet.

347
00:28:32,659 --> 00:28:37,467
We know poetry, in all its symmetrical forms and what he speaks is not poetry.

348
00:28:37,956 --> 00:28:42,338
Al-Waleed Bin Mugheera(الوليد بن مغيره) in another narration says, I am the most expert among you, in poetry,

349
00:28:42,752 --> 00:28:46,814
I know all of its forms, and Qur'an is not poetry.

350
00:28:48,301 --> 00:28:51,317
They said: Let's claim that he is a sorcerer.

351
00:28:51,730 --> 00:29:00,037
He said: No! He is no sorcerer, we've seen sorcerers and their magic, and he doesn't do any of their tying and untying.

352
00:29:01,406 --> 00:29:04,231
So, basically, they mentioned all, what they have

353
00:29:04,740 --> 00:29:08,936
and Al-Waleed Bin Mugheera(الوليد بن مغيرة) is saying that this won't make sense.

354
00:29:09,690 --> 00:29:11,097
Eventually, they said;

355
00:29:11,595 --> 00:29:12,964
Well, what are we gonna say.

356
00:29:13,956 --> 00:29:16,909
So, he thought about it for a while and then he came back and said,

357
00:29:17,213 --> 00:29:19,543
well, let's just say that he's a sorcerer.

358
00:29:20,753 --> 00:29:26,279
Before that he said: By God, there is splendor in what he speaks

359
00:29:26,562 --> 00:29:30,729
in essence, he is like a palm tree, whose branches give much fruit.

360
00:29:31,621 --> 00:29:35,286
All you have been saying will not be believed.

361
00:29:36,206 --> 00:29:38,475
The closest thing is for you, to say,

362
00:29:38,840 --> 00:29:42,570
This man is a sorcerer, who comes between a man and his religion,

363
00:29:42,891 --> 00:29:44,200
a man and his father,

364
00:29:44,347 --> 00:29:45,546
a man and his wife,

365
00:29:45,760 --> 00:29:46,893
a man and his brother,

366
00:29:47,080 --> 00:29:48,340
and a man and his tribe.

367
00:29:48,856 --> 00:29:54,129
That's the closest that we can come to agree on that he's a sorcerer.

368
00:29:56,297 --> 00:29:58,709
That is when Allah سبحانه وتعالى revealed the Ayaat(آيات)

369
00:29:59,544 --> 00:30:02,894
ذَرْنِي وَمَنْ خَلَقْتُ وَحِيدًا۝

370
00:30:03,134 --> 00:30:07,105
وَجَعَلْتُ لَهُ مَالًا مَمْدُودًا۝

371
00:30:07,336 --> 00:30:09,669
 وَبَنِينَ شُهُودًا۝

372
00:30:09,969 --> 00:30:13,103
وَمَهَّدْتُ لَهُ تَمْهِيدًا۝

373
00:30:13,397 --> 00:30:17,792
 ثُمَّ يَطْمَعُ أَنْ أَزِيدَ۝

374
00:30:18,238 --> 00:30:24,867
كَلَّا ۖ إِنَّهُ كَانَ لِآيَاتِنَا عَنِيدًا۝

375
00:30:25,312 --> 00:30:27,984
سَأُرْهِقُهُ صَعُودًا ۝

376
00:30:28,321 --> 00:30:31,251
إِنَّهُ فَكَّرَ وَقَدَّرَ ۝

377
00:30:31,503 --> 00:30:33,626
 فَقُتِلَ كَيْفَ قَدَّرَ ۝

378
00:30:33,963 --> 00:30:36,809
  ثُمَّ قُتِلَ كَيْفَ قَدَّرَ ۝

379
00:30:37,184 --> 00:30:38,737
ثُمَّ نَظَرَ  ۝

380
00:30:39,054 --> 00:30:41,160
ثُمَّ عَبَسَ وَبَسَرَ ۝

381
00:30:41,475 --> 00:30:44,073
 ثُمَّ أَدْبَرَ وَاسْتَكْبَرَ ۝َ

382
00:30:44,358 --> 00:30:51,107
فَقَالَ إِنْ هَٰذَا إِلَّا سِحْرٌ يُؤْثَرُ۝

383
00:30:52,011 --> 00:30:54,203
Verily, he thought and plotted.

384
00:30:54,482 --> 00:30:56,922
So, let him be cursed, how he plotted.

385
00:30:57,445 --> 00:31:00,570
And once more, let him be cursed how he plotted.

386
00:31:00,948 --> 00:31:05,424
Then he thought, then he fround and he looked in a bad tempered way.

387
00:31:05,774 --> 00:31:07,698
Then he turned back and was proud.

388
00:31:07,970 --> 00:31:11,856
Then he said, this is nothing but magic from that of old.

389
00:31:12,176 --> 00:31:14,721
This is nothing but the word of a human being.

390
00:31:16,350 --> 00:31:18,853
These Ayaat(آيات) are in Surah Al-Mudassir(سورة ألمدثر).

391
00:31:20,039 --> 00:31:23,302
Number four: Deforming the message.

392
00:31:24,136 --> 00:31:31,481
An-Nadhar Bin Hariss(النضر بن حارث), he went to Persia, specifically to learn stories.

393
00:31:32,000 --> 00:31:34,272
He went all the way to Persia to learn stories.

394
00:31:35,835 --> 00:31:42,091
He came back and whenever he would see Rasool Allah ﷺ sitting with a group of people.

395
00:31:42,798 --> 00:31:47,979
He would call the people and call others and say: Come to me, I have better stories to tell.

396
00:31:49,085 --> 00:31:50,325
My stories are better.

397
00:31:51,696 --> 00:31:59,131
And he was saying it's all about stories, what Muhammadﷺ is speaking about the past all of this, these are just fables, tales.

398
00:31:59,743 --> 00:32:01,345
I have something better to offer.

399
00:32:01,815 --> 00:32:03,256
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

400
00:32:04,169 --> 00:32:10,057
وَقَالُوا أَسَاطِيرُ الْأَوَّلِينَ اكْتَتَبَهَا

401
00:32:10,701 --> 00:32:16,616
فَهِيَ تُمْلَىٰ عَلَيْهِ بُكْرَةً وَأَصِيلًا۝

402
00:32:17,833 --> 00:32:22,041
They claim that these are stories or Tales of the past.

403
00:32:22,858 --> 00:32:29,427
So, they wanted to say that this is just storytelling, tales that are fabricated, untrue.

404
00:32:30,388 --> 00:32:35,808
Who knows what happened to Musaعليه السّلام, who knows what happened to Eesa(عيسى), who knows what happened to the other Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

405
00:32:36,140 --> 00:32:37,817
He's just telling you stories.

406
00:32:38,306 --> 00:32:42,162
There is no basis of what he is narrating to you.

407
00:32:43,478 --> 00:32:47,376
Number five: Bargaining and negotiations;

408
00:32:48,577 --> 00:32:51,811
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) came to Muhammadﷺ and said;

409
00:32:52,541 --> 00:32:53,559
Let's make a deal.

410
00:32:54,604 --> 00:33:01,149
We will agree to worship Allah for one day and you worship our gods for another day.

411
00:33:01,737 --> 00:33:06,883
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them, I would never agree to do such a thing.

412
00:33:07,608 --> 00:33:12,109
They came back to him sometime later, and they said: We have a better offer to make.

413
00:33:12,799 --> 00:33:17,880
We will worship Allah for a week, and you worship our gods for one day.

414
00:33:19,427 --> 00:33:20,343
He said: No.

415
00:33:21,689 --> 00:33:24,521
Came back again, we have a better offer to make.

416
00:33:25,239 --> 00:33:30,215
We will worship Allah for a month and you just give us one day.

417
00:33:30,995 --> 00:33:32,214
Rasool Ullah said: No

418
00:33:33,398 --> 00:33:35,046
Allah سبحانه وتعالى revealed the Ayah(آية).

419
00:33:35,095 --> 00:33:37,029
وَدُّوا لَوْ تُدْهِنُ فَيُدْهِنُونَ۝

420
00:33:37,813 --> 00:33:42,432
They would wish that you would compromise, so that they can compromise with you.

421
00:33:43,294 --> 00:33:47,045
Their religion is manmade, they could compromise in it, they can change it.

422
00:33:47,171 --> 00:33:50,246
It's okay for them to worship Allah for a day and their gods for another day.

423
00:33:50,468 --> 00:33:53,240
It's fine, it's a man made religion, there's no control on it.

424
00:33:54,014 --> 00:33:57,014
But Rasool Allah ﷺ is receiving Wahee(وحي) from Allah, he cannot change it.

425
00:33:58,172 --> 00:33:59,812
So, he cannot compromise in the message.

426
00:34:00,828 --> 00:34:02,209
The message doesn't change.

427
00:34:03,431 --> 00:34:06,399
Even if you worship Allah for a year, I'm not going to give you one day.

428
00:34:06,897 --> 00:34:08,710
I'm not going to give you a day in my whole life.

429
00:34:09,266 --> 00:34:14,510
قُلْ يَا أَيُّهَا الْكَافِرُونَ۝

430
00:34:14,867 --> 00:34:20,485
لَا أَعْبُدُ مَا تَعْبُدُونَ۝

431
00:34:21,271 --> 00:34:26,953
O you, disbelievers, I am not gonna worship what you worship, neither are you going to worship, what I worship.

432
00:34:27,877 --> 00:34:32,576
لَكُمْ دِينُكُمْ وَلِيَ دِينِ۝

433
00:34:33,005 --> 00:34:35,048
You have your way and I have mine

434
00:34:36,602 --> 00:34:41,931
And they tried all different ways of bargaining, it would never work with Muhammadﷺ.

435
00:34:43,348 --> 00:34:47,395
Now they would become upset because this is something that, they could afford to do

436
00:34:48,166 --> 00:34:51,227
and they were wondering how come Rasool Allah ﷺ can't do it.

437
00:34:52,207 --> 00:34:57,996
Why do we have to always keep on compromising and bargaining and he is not reciprocating.

438
00:34:59,305 --> 00:35:03,269
And that was a cause of obviously that aggravated them further.

439
00:35:03,700 --> 00:35:08,584
But Muhammad ﷺ was telling them that I am just a conveyor of a message.

440
00:35:09,003 --> 00:35:11,464
It is not from myself, it is from Allah.

441
00:35:12,960 --> 00:35:18,080
6; Allurements and temptations, and Number Seven, Setting Challenges,

442
00:35:18,301 --> 00:35:22,953
This following narration points out to both number six and seven.

443
00:35:23,773 --> 00:35:25,889
It's a narration by Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ),

444
00:35:26,853 --> 00:35:31,037
Ibn Abbasرضي الله عنه said that the leaders from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) met

445
00:35:31,604 --> 00:35:36,472
and they were next to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) and they said let's send for Muhammad(محمد) and speak with him.

446
00:35:37,025 --> 00:35:43,232
And we want to exhaust all different ways and we don't want to give him any excuse.

447
00:35:43,358 --> 00:35:45,424
Let's try everything with him.

448
00:35:46,063 --> 00:35:49,804
So, they sent someone to call Muhammadﷺ.

449
00:35:50,534 --> 00:35:56,175
Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) says; that Muhammadﷺ came rushing, he was eager to come and meet with the leaders

450
00:35:56,215 --> 00:35:59,365
because he thought there might be a change of heart.

451
00:36:00,173 --> 00:36:04,742
Maybe now they want to respond, maybe they're willing to soften their stance.

452
00:36:05,129 --> 00:36:07,502
So, he came to them in a hurry.

453
00:36:08,482 --> 00:36:13,476
When he arrived there, Utba(عتبه) started speaking to Muhammadﷺ,

454
00:36:14,462 --> 00:36:18,578
actually Utba(عتبه) was one of them, but there were many around all of the leaders.

455
00:36:19,177 --> 00:36:21,297
They told Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه

456
00:36:21,337 --> 00:36:25,336
O Muhammad(محمد), we sent for you to reconcile with you.

457
00:36:25,908 --> 00:36:29,559
So, it started with this very nice statement.

458
00:36:30,293 --> 00:36:34,473
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was getting an impression that finally they're softening.

459
00:36:35,088 --> 00:36:38,923
They said: O Muhammad, we sent for you to reconcile with you,

460
00:36:39,069 --> 00:36:46,199
by God, we know of no Arab man who has ever brought his people as much trouble as you have.

461
00:36:47,571 --> 00:36:51,390
You have reviled the forbearers, criticize the religion,

462
00:36:51,853 --> 00:36:56,648
 ridiculed the values, cursed the gods, and divided our community.

463
00:36:57,121 --> 00:37:02,833
Every unpleasant thing possible you have done to make a rift, between you and us.

464
00:37:04,535 --> 00:37:12,322
In another narration, they said: We have never seen a person, who has brought so much evil on his people like you have.

465
00:37:13,643 --> 00:37:17,821
And now they're starting to throw out the temptations to Muhammadﷺ.

466
00:37:18,086 --> 00:37:23,774
They said: O Muhammad(محمد) if you are presenting us with this message,

467
00:37:23,837 --> 00:37:31,432
 because you are in need of money, we will collect for you money, until we make you the wealthiest among us.

468
00:37:33,063 --> 00:37:40,285
O Muhammad(محمد), If you are coming up with this religion, because you are seeking power,

469
00:37:40,766 --> 00:37:43,308
we will appoint you as a king over us.

470
00:37:44,935 --> 00:37:51,998
O Muhammad(محمد), If you are presenting us with this religion, because you are desiring women,

471
00:37:52,522 --> 00:37:57,761
we will choose for you the best 10 women in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and marry them all to you.

472
00:37:58,648 --> 00:38:05,734
O Muhammad(محمد), if you are presenting us with this message, because you are obsessed with devils, demons;

473
00:38:06,128 --> 00:38:16,022
We will spend whatever is needed to cure you, even if we have to exhaust all of our wealth in the process.

474
00:38:17,676 --> 00:38:18,730
Tell us what you want?

475
00:38:19,813 --> 00:38:25,929
Rasool Allah ﷺ responded and said, what you have said, does not apply to me.

476
00:38:26,491 --> 00:38:33,032
I have not brought to you my message seeking your money, nor honor among you, nor sovereignty over you.

477
00:38:33,700 --> 00:38:35,885
God has sent me to you as a messenger

478
00:38:36,373 --> 00:38:41,273
He has revealed the document to me and has ordered me to bring you good news and warn you.

479
00:38:41,786 --> 00:38:45,252
I have brought you a message from my Lord, and I've given you counsel.

480
00:38:45,734 --> 00:38:52,255
If you accept what I've brought to you, then that is for your good on earth, and in the hereafter,

481
00:38:52,374 --> 00:38:58,310
 if you reject it, I will await God's decision, until he decides between myself and you.

482
00:38:59,846 --> 00:39:02,999
These are the approximate words of Muhammadﷺ.

483
00:39:04,470 --> 00:39:09,504
They said: Alright, if you are turning down all of our offers

484
00:39:10,224 --> 00:39:14,284
then, you know how narrow our land is.

485
00:39:14,344 --> 00:39:16,654
You know, for those of you have seen Makkah.

486
00:39:17,015 --> 00:39:22,188
Makkah is very narrow valleys surrounded by mountains you know, mountains all over.

487
00:39:22,942 --> 00:39:30,955
And it's a very rough environment, the weather of it and all of these mountains, and it is very narrow.

488
00:39:31,255 --> 00:39:36,313
 So, they said: O Muhammad(محمد), you know how narrow our land is,

489
00:39:37,254 --> 00:39:41,674
and how poor we are, and how difficult our life is.

490
00:39:42,647 --> 00:39:45,654
So, how about you go to your Lord, who has sent you,

491
00:39:46,845 --> 00:39:49,051
and you tell him to move these mountains away,

492
00:39:50,288 --> 00:39:52,779
just level them and give us more space and land.

493
00:39:53,682 --> 00:39:59,097
And then why don't you ask him to make some rivers flow in Makkah, like the rivers of Syria and Iraq.

494
00:39:59,423 --> 00:40:02,223
We want to have some rivers like other people have.

495
00:40:03,969 --> 00:40:10,641
And then we want you also to go to your Lord and to tell Him to bring back to life, some of our forefathers.

496
00:40:11,802 --> 00:40:17,761
And we want you to bring back to life Qusa'e Bin Kulaab(قصئ بن كلاب) because he was a truth telling Shaikh(شيخ).

497
00:40:18,136 --> 00:40:22,270
And we want to ask him, if what you are saying is true or not.

498
00:40:23,544 --> 00:40:31,110
And then Muhammad(محمد) if you do that, and our forefathers, agree to what you say, then will follow you.

499
00:40:32,787 --> 00:40:38,211
Muhammadﷺ responded and said, this is not why I have been sent.

500
00:40:38,865 --> 00:40:42,440
I have only brought you from God what He has sent me with,

501
00:40:42,951 --> 00:40:47,609
I have informed you of what I was sent to convey to you, If you accept it

502
00:40:48,016 --> 00:40:51,763
then that is your good fortune on earth, and in the hereafter.

503
00:40:51,874 --> 00:40:57,269
If you reject it, I must wait patiently for God's decree and for him to judge between us.

504
00:40:58,906 --> 00:41:04,659
They continued and they said: Well, how about if you then, ask your Lord

505
00:41:05,430 --> 00:41:09,178
to send down an angel, who will witness to your truth

506
00:41:09,851 --> 00:41:19,034
and also we want you to ask him to give us some castles, gardens, treasures of gold and silver.

507
00:41:19,524 --> 00:41:21,237
And then how about you do this?

508
00:41:22,314 --> 00:41:28,830
Why don't you tell Him to fulfill your needs because we see that you are seeking a livelihood just like we are, you doing business.

509
00:41:29,308 --> 00:41:31,387
Now, if you are so close to your God

510
00:41:31,835 --> 00:41:37,506
why don't you tell him to give you some wealth, so that we'll know how prestigious you are, in His eyes.

511
00:41:38,829 --> 00:41:40,831
That is if you're claiming to be a messenger,

512
00:41:41,444 --> 00:41:44,090
how come you're just like every one of us, you going and working.

513
00:41:44,814 --> 00:41:47,208
Tell your Lord if He loves you to give you some Wealth.

514
00:41:48,207 --> 00:41:51,139
Again, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I'm not going to do so,

515
00:41:51,482 --> 00:41:54,082
I am not the one to ask such things of His Lord.

516
00:41:54,479 --> 00:41:56,646
That is not why I have been sent to you

517
00:41:56,975 --> 00:41:59,242
God has sent me to announce and warn.

518
00:41:59,587 --> 00:42:05,848
If you accept my message then that is your good fortune here on Earth and in the Afterlife.

519
00:42:06,067 --> 00:42:09,804
If you reject it then I must be patient and leave the matter up to God,

520
00:42:10,098 --> 00:42:13,668
until He decides between myself and you.

521
00:42:14,092 --> 00:42:15,329
They said: Well, then fine.

522
00:42:16,091 --> 00:42:20,351
Ask your Lord to bring down the punishment that you have been promising us.

523
00:42:20,832 --> 00:42:23,843
Come on! Let him bring the sky upon our heads right now.

524
00:42:24,203 --> 00:42:25,383
Show us if you can.

525
00:42:25,675 --> 00:42:29,760
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: That is up to God, if, He wishes, He will do that to you.

526
00:42:31,576 --> 00:42:38,074
They commented and said: O Muhammad(محمد), doesn't your Lord know these questions that we're going to ask you?

527
00:42:38,275 --> 00:42:40,824
How come is not helping you and giving you an answer.

528
00:42:42,424 --> 00:42:44,356
We know who's teaching you all of this.

529
00:42:44,929 --> 00:42:51,817
You are being taught this Qur'an of yours, by a man in Yamamah(يمامه) called Ar-Rahman(الرحمن).

530
00:42:52,824 --> 00:42:55,511
And we're never gonna believe in that man called Ar-Rahman(الرحمن).

531
00:42:56,492 --> 00:42:59,060
All of it, just fabricating lies one over another,

532
00:42:59,100 --> 00:43:03,136
this man in Yamamah(يمامه) called Ar-Rahman(الرحمن), something they made up and fabricated.

533
00:43:04,405 --> 00:43:07,448
One of them said: We worship the angels who are God's daughters,

534
00:43:07,897 --> 00:43:12,128
another said: we will not believe you till you bring us God and the angels beforehand.

535
00:43:12,438 --> 00:43:16,642
It's all mockery and insults, and then they left.

536
00:43:17,519 --> 00:43:21,622
One of them came back, to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

537
00:43:22,793 --> 00:43:28,372
So, one might think that this man, Abdullah Bin Umayyah(عبدالله بن أمية) felt sorry for what happened.

538
00:43:29,206 --> 00:43:31,348
And maybe you wanted to come and apologize

539
00:43:32,035 --> 00:43:34,141
Or maybe he wanted to come and become Muslim.

540
00:43:35,200 --> 00:43:40,434
Specially that he is a cousin of Rasool Allah ﷺ, his mother is Rasool Ullah's aunt.

541
00:43:41,758 --> 00:43:44,593
Well, Abdullah Bin Umayyah(عبدالله بن أميه) came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said:

542
00:43:45,112 --> 00:43:52,464
O Muhammad(محمد), your people have offered you the best offers, and you turned them down.

543
00:43:53,417 --> 00:43:58,179
And then they asked you to perform miracles for them, and you refused.

544
00:43:58,913 --> 00:44:02,589
They asked you to bring down punishment on them, and you didn't.

545
00:44:03,212 --> 00:44:04,228
Now I'll tell you what?

546
00:44:05,141 --> 00:44:12,288
I'm not gonna believe in you, until you bring a ladder that goes all the way up to the heaven.

547
00:44:13,194 --> 00:44:16,766
And then you climb it, while I'm watching you,

548
00:44:17,982 --> 00:44:19,986
and you go up to God, to Allah,

549
00:44:20,852 --> 00:44:23,344
and you asked him to write down for you a letter,

550
00:44:23,959 --> 00:44:28,463
stating that you are His Prophet, and have Him sign it,

551
00:44:29,732 --> 00:44:35,101
and then we want that document to come down accompanied by four angels,

552
00:44:36,221 --> 00:44:38,939
to be witnesses that you are a messenger from God.

553
00:44:40,894 --> 00:44:43,910
And then you know what, even if you do that

554
00:44:44,505 --> 00:44:48,100
I think I'm not gonna believe in you, Dead End!!!

555
00:44:48,979 --> 00:44:50,685
Nothing is going to work with these people.

556
00:44:51,386 --> 00:44:53,778
وَإِنْ يَرَوْا كُلَّ آيَةٍ لَا يُؤْمِنُوا بِهَا

557
00:44:54,042 --> 00:44:56,519
If they see every sign they won't believe.

558
00:44:57,649 --> 00:45:02,886
This was the environment Rasool Allah ﷺ was working in, dealing with these type of people.

559
00:45:04,434 --> 00:45:12,954
It's a Dead End you can go any further, whatever you're going to do, I'm telling you beforehand, I'm not gonna believe.

560
00:45:14,013 --> 00:45:21,173
Even if Allah sends down a message from Him personally with four angels to witness it, it's not going to be enough.

561
00:45:23,107 --> 00:45:27,502
Rasool Allah ﷺ went back home, he was regretful,

562
00:45:28,540 --> 00:45:31,884
at the failure to achieve what he had expected from his people

563
00:45:31,924 --> 00:45:37,338
because he went with all of his good expectation, that now my people have changed.

564
00:45:38,121 --> 00:45:40,784
That was the impression he got when they invited him.

565
00:45:41,277 --> 00:45:45,020
And then suddenly he was turned down in this ruthless fashion.

566
00:45:46,941 --> 00:45:49,549
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

